{
  "inShort": "No gameplay or new artifacts were shown, so what got built this sprint is unknown. The goal is behind on evidence: halfway through the checkpoint, nothing openable demonstrates the islands, tide loop, co-op sailing or five-player test.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x0600jscsz8r4935jty",
      "text": "The repository evidence matches the task: public Godot demos, an MIT license and import instructions. It closes the reference task, not a playable part of your game."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x0s00jtcsz8az0lkwpy",
      "text": "The animated reference remains done. Only the Big Buck Bunny title and thumbnail were inspected, so the animation itself remains unverified. Reusing this link in the devlog does not demonstrate your game's progress."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x1800jucsz8wothj7j8",
      "text": "The inspected article explains playtesting and matches the reference task. It supplies reading material, not evidence that five players tested the slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x1q00jvcsz8qpwzz58f",
      "text": "The private design board closes a planning task. Nothing shown this sprint connects it to a playable tide loop or sailing route."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [
    "cmvun2x2600jwcsz8e6von2yr"
  ],
  "outsidePlan": [
    "The devlog reports a second island and reef damage. The second island would advance the checkpoint goal, despite not belonging to a listed task. Neither claim is demonstrated: the image shows a mountain landscape, and the video preview identifies Big Buck Bunny."
  ],
  "questions": [
    "Does an openable build contain both islands, flooding and draining, and two-player sailing?",
    "Have five players tested that build, and what could they complete?",
    "Does the trailer storyboard still belong in this checkpoint's plan?"
  ],
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "Devlog #2 announced another island and reef damage, with 0 applause and 0 views; the project lists no store page or game link.",
    "team": "The stated 10–15 hours a week covers Alex only, so total capacity remains unknown. Mia did not confirm week-two work, leaving her availability for the remaining programming unconfirmed.",
    "management": "Halfway through 28 days, four setup or reference tasks are closed, but none demonstrates the playable-slice goal. Publishing the prototype devlog meets the stage's sole formal requirement, but does not establish a proven core or player-tested progress toward release."
  }
}

